1
00:00:00,274 --> 00:00:12,786
A signed fictional refund event enters a durable PostgreSQL inbox. Acceptance is separate from successful processing.

2
00:00:12,786 --> 00:00:25,721
Three identical redeliveries return the original receipt. The event still has one processing attempt and one local completion.

3
00:00:25,721 --> 00:00:39,823
Version 2 was applied before version 1 arrived. The older snapshot is recorded as stale; the completed projection stays at version 2.

4
00:00:39,823 --> 00:00:55,404
This fictional handler keeps failing. Automatic retries have a bounded budget and preserve every attempt.

5
00:00:55,404 --> 00:01:02,975
The operator repairs the demo cause, then requests replay with a reason. Repair alone does not rewrite or restart the accepted event.

6
00:01:02,975 --> 00:01:21,389
Replay succeeded in a new processing cycle. The original receipt and bytes are unchanged, all three failures remain, and exactly one local completion exists.
